The {{Nihongo|Okami Imperial University|大紙帝国大学|Okami Teikoku Daigaku}}, often abbreviated as Shidai (紙大) or OIU, is a public research university located in [[Okami]], [[Okaiken]]. Founded in 1877, it is the oldest and largest of the national universities in Okaiken. The institution is widely considered the most prestigious university in the country and consistently ranks at the top of national academic league tables. 

Unlike institutions within the Gakushuin system, which historically catered to the nobility, Okami Imperial University was established as a meritocratic institution aimed at modernizing the nation and cultivating leaders across all sectors of society. 

==History==
The university was chartered by the Imperial government in April 1877, merging several older government schools of medicine and Western learning. During its initial decades as a modern institution, Okadai benefited from the contributions of international scholars who helped establish its core faculties of Law, Science, Literature, and Medicine. 

The main campus in the central ward of Okami is built on the former estate of prominent feudal lord [[Inuyama Masahide]]. It is notable for its historic architecture, much of which survived the turbulent periods of the 20th century. The iconic main gate, often referred to as the Crimson Gate, and the grand central auditorium are registered national cultural heritage properties.

==Campuses==
The university operates three core campuses within the Greater Okami area, along with dozens of research facilities spread across the nation.

The Central Okami Campus houses the traditional faculties, the main administrative buildings, and the grand library. It is the historic heart of the university and is characterized by tree-lined avenues and brick facades.

The Tatara Campus, located further north, is home to the College of Arts and Sciences. All undergraduate students spend their first two years at this campus undergoing a liberal arts education before moving to the Central Campus to specialize in their chosen fields.

The Eastern Kaimi Campus is a modern addition focused on advanced scientific research, environmental studies, and interdisciplinary sciences.

==Academics==
Okami Imperial University consists of 10 faculties and 15 graduate schools. It enrolls approximately 28,500 students, roughly evenly divided between undergraduate and postgraduate programs. The university is a highly selective institution, with an acceptance rate typically hovering around a single digit for its most competitive programs.

The university operates on a unique two-tier system for undergraduates. Students are initially admitted to the College of Arts and Sciences for a two-year liberal arts curriculum. Following this, they transition to one of the specialized senior faculties for their final two years of study. 

The institution is also home to 11 affiliated research institutes, covering disciplines ranging from earthquake research to advanced medical sciences. The university library system is the largest in Okaiken, housing over 10 million volumes.

